Z||000000||b lo 0||03-10-2001||03:25 PM||||Alright, here goes.  '85 GT 3spd Auto...<BR>When car is warmed up and I gun it taking a corner from a stop and sometimes straight uphill, fuel pump fuse blows.  Sometimes while driving down the road, fuel pump will cut off, engine will die, and start up again by itself.  This happens ALL THE TIME.  I think it's the fuel press. sensor, not sure.  Also, if I floor it, she will NOT rev past about 4k rpm.  However, if I shift manually and barely press the gas, it revs to 5k.  Also, she has enough bottom end, but kinda runs out of power around 3k.  Revs really fast when in park, tho.  WTH is going on with my car???  I'd really like to know.  Thnx, guys and gals.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT (in progress)  <BR>titled ICE-plates B LO 0 <BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.angelfire.com/ga3/audioimagery/ice.gif">     <BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.audioimagery.i-p.com" TARGET=_blank>www.audioimagery.i-p.com</A>  !!!<P><A HREF="http://clubs.excite.com/welcome/main?cid=.zXb1DJ1lsCL&aid=22&auth=" TARGET=_blank>Pontiac Fiero Owner's Club</A>-Pics, Videos and More-Or Post your Own||||reg||1
Z||000001||MontanaFiero||03-10-2001||03:40 PM||||Better replace your fuel pump before you get stranded. That's what my '87 was doing. I ignored it, then one day I ended up towing it from WalMart and dropping the fuel tank in my parking lot.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg">   <BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- <I>project</I> &lt;&lt;||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||03-10-2001||08:20 PM||||A similiar problem with my 88. Change the fuse, do a little power acceleration andthefuse would blow.  A real intermittant problem. After 2 new fuel pumps, 2 new fuel rails at Mr. Goodwrench, Twin Lakes Fiero located a short in the wiring harness where it was rubbing on the heat shield shorting out the fuel pump circuit and blowing the fuel pump fuse.<P>Check out the wire harness cable on the left side of the engine, back near the fire wall for any chafing.<P>The fuel pump circuit itself has only two wires: one for the fuel pump, the other for the oil sending unit.<P>A real pain of a fix.||||reg||3
