Z||000004||1FST2M6||03-14-2001||04:58 PM||||how many miles does your car have on it? your fuel pressure regulator may need to be rebuilt.. NAPA has a kit.. and it'll take about an hour...  but a bad regulator will flow fuel straight through and dead heead the pump which can cause the fuse to pop.. my nitrous car did that.. ti'll i just wired through the fuse.. but i need the extra fuel pressure.. you don't. check too see if the vacuum hose on the FPR is still there.. or if it's split..<P><BR>oh.. Look for some of the Fiero Guys on WSB Channel 2 satuday about 1-2:30  we'll be in the St. Patties day parade through downtown..||||reg||1
Z||000005||b lo 0||03-15-2001||12:59 PM||||150,672.8 mi<P>I'll be watchin for you guys Sat.  Sorry I can't come!  I wanted to go SOOOO bad!  Oh, btw, fuel starvation is now beginning-so I'm pretty sure it's the pump,  I have a new one, going in Sunday.  Now how about that rev limit problem?  It's killin me!!  Thank you Montana, Lar and Trav for your help.<P>PS-Trav, maybe I can make it to the next meeting, but if not, whaddya say we go cruise one weekend?  I'd love to ride in a nitro SE!  BTW, I installed a circuit breaker in the place of the fuel pump fuse for ease of resetting and antitheft (no flowie da fuel, no movie da car) and the fire extenguisher was successfully mounted under the dash in the passenger footwell.||||reg||1
